        <div id="who-should-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Buy Pro JYM, and Who Should Skip It?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Pro JYM is best for lifters who want one all-day protein that works after training and before bed, and who like thick, dessert-style shakes. It is a poor fit for drug-tested athletes, for anyone avoiding artificial sweeteners who will not switch to the Natural version, and for buyers who only want the cheapest protein per gram.
          </p>

          <p>
            Buy it if you drink two shakes a day, one after training and one later in the evening, and do not want to keep separate whey and casein tubs. The casein-leaning blend makes sense there, and at about $1.74 per 25 g in the big tub it is not much more expensive than buying whey and casein separately. It also suits people who use a shake as a snack between meals, because the thicker, slower-digesting blend tends to feel more filling than whey.
          </p>

          <p>
            Skip it if you compete in a tested sport, because JYM claims no sport certification. Skip it if you are lactose sensitive, because the casein and milk protein isolate carry more lactose than an isolate; Iso JYM or an isolate is the better choice. And skip it if all you want is a quick post-workout shake at the lowest price, where a whey from our <a href="/best-whey-protein-powder/">best whey protein powder</a> list will do the job for less.
          </p>

          <p>
            A word on health: a 24 g protein shake is a normal food for most healthy adults. Anyone with kidney disease, anyone who is pregnant or nursing, and anyone taking prescription medication should check with a doctor or registered dietitian before adding protein supplements, which is also what the Pro JYM label itself advises. The label also says it is not for people under 18 without professional advice. If you are unsure how much protein you need in the first place, start with our <a href="/how-much-protein-do-i-need/">protein calculator guide</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

