                  Buyers and reviewers most often praise Chocolate Mousse, and JYM promotes Chocolate Cookie Crunch and S'mores as award-winning flavors. Tahitian Vanilla Bean is described by some buyers as mild, which makes it a good base for oats and smoothies but less exciting with water. If you are unsure, try a 22-serving tub before buying a 45-serving one.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are the most common Pro JYM complaints?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The common complaints are price, an artificial sweetener aftertaste in some flavors, a mild vanilla, and small clumps if you mix with a spoon instead of a shaker. Some buyers also note that it is thicker than they expected from a whey product. Praise centers on the chocolate flavors, the creamy texture and the transparent label.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Who makes Pro JYM, and where is it made?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Pro JYM is sold by JYM Supplement Science, the brand owned by Jim Stoppani, PhD. The label lists PHD Fitness in Westlake Village, California, as the distributor and says the product is made in the USA with domestic and international ingredients, in a GMP-certified facility. Pro JYM is sold on JYM's own site, on Amazon and through other retailers.
                </p>
              </div>
